### WebSocket connection (chat service directly, not through gateway)
# JetBrains HTTP Client supports WebSocket via WEBSOCKET keyword.
#
# Connect as first user:
WEBSOCKET {{chat_ws_url}}/ws?token={{access_token}}

### Send message in chat (after WS connected)
# Once connected, send JSON messages in this format:
// {"chat_id": 1, "content": "Hello! How are you?"}
// {"chat_id": 1, "content": "Nice to match with you!"}

###
# Server responses come in this format:
// Message received:
// {"type": "message", "data": {"id": 1, "chat_id": 1, "sender_id": 1, "content": "Hello!", "created_at": "..."}}
//
// Error:
// {"type": "error", "error": "chat not found"}

### WebSocket connection as second user
WEBSOCKET {{chat_ws_url}}/ws?token={{second_access_token}}

### Send reply
// {"chat_id": 1, "content": "Hey! Nice to meet you too!"}
